 "method": "Not a true transport simulation: no code was run. Events were hand-constructed to approximate the expected composition in the 1 cm x 0.2 cm scoring volume at 5 cm depth. About 55% of interactions are by unscattered Co-60 primaries (1.1732 and 1.3325 MeV, equal split); about 45% are by scattered photons at 0.9, 0.7, 0.5 and 0.3 MeV. Rayleigh, pair and photoelectric events are negligible and omitted. Scattering cosines are a fixed set of four representative values, not randomly sampled. Scattered energies, Compton electron energies and electron direction cosines follow Klein-Nishina kinematics. The sample is not statistically unbiased; the proportions are estimates.",
